  "abstract": "Experienced faculty have acceptable inter-rater reliability when using PhaBS, consistent with other behaviour marker systems; however, not all raters are competent. Competence measures for other assessments can be helpfully applied to behavioural marker systems. When using behavioural marker systems for assessment, educators must start using such rater competence frameworks. This is important to ensure fair and accurate assessments for learners, to provide educators with information about rater training programmes, and to provide individual raters with meaningful feedback.",
